# Normalize text files across platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Common ROM/media/build artifacts should stay binary if they ever appear
# locally; the release guards still forbid committing them.
*.z64 binary
*.n64 binary
*.v64 binary
*.rom binary
*.bin binary
*.bmp binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.raw binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ogg binary
*.flac binary
*.dmg binary
*.zip binary
*.7z binary
*.tar binary
*.tgz binary
*.gz binary

# Keep GitHub language statistics focused on mdkr64-owned code. These are the
# build-time vendored dependencies documented in NOTICE.md (retained for build
# compatibility, each under its own upstream license). MGB64's equivalent list
# (tools/armips.cpp, tools/asm-processor/**, tools/extractor/*, tools/gzipsrc/**,
# tools/smaa/*, tools/ido5.3_recomp/**, tools/mktex/**) has no counterpart here —
# mdkr64 vendors only these two.
lib/glad/** linguist-vendored
lib/sdl_gamecontrollerdb/** linguist-vendored

# --- Internal working documentation: the public/internal boundary ------------
#
# The paths below are internal working material and are NOT published.
#
#   docs/superpowers/**  -- internal planning workspace (plans/, specs/); not
#                           part of the public docs/ reference surface.
#   PUBLIC_LAUNCH_BACKLOG.md -- internal public-launch program tracking doc.
#   docs/archive/**      -- the dated working documents (implementation reports,
#                           audits, censuses, design studies, reviews) that this
#                           port accumulated while it was built.
#   docs/SDK_INVENTORY.md -- the historical legend-bearing-file inventory.
#
# HOW THEY ARE ACTUALLY EXCLUDED, and what these lines do and do not do.
#
# The public release is a SQUASHED single-commit cut pushed to a separate public
# repository; this repository stays private. The paths above are removed from
# that cut with `git rm` before the commit is made, so they are absent from the
# public tree AND from its history. That deletion is the mechanism. It is not
# optional and it is not implemented here.
#
# The `export-ignore` attributes below only affect `git archive`, i.e. tarballs
# and zips generated from this repository. They are kept as a second layer for
# that one path. They have no effect on clone, fetch, push, or on the release
# cut. Do not cite this file as the reason any of the above is unpublished.
#
# Everything directly under docs/ that is not listed here is public by
# construction.
docs/superpowers/** export-ignore
PUBLIC_LAUNCH_BACKLOG.md export-ignore
docs/archive/** export-ignore
docs/SDK_INVENTORY.md export-ignore
